  "title": "JPSC-JSSC Reform Manch suspends agitation amid Jharkhand government's exam cancellations",
  "summary": "The Jharkhand government cancels 22 recruitment exams, including those by the Jharkhand Public Service Commission and an outsourced agency, after protests and a 2-month ultimatum to the government. The reform movement, led by JPSC-JSSC Reform Manch, claims the cancellation is a response to systemic issues in the exam process.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Jharkhand government cancels 22 recruitment exams, including those by the Jharkhand Public Service Commission (JPSC) and an outsourced agency.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The government announces a 2-month ultimatum to the state government to address the exam irregularities and conduct a fair probe.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "JPSC-JSSC Reform Manch led by Ravindra Paswan claims the cancellation is a response to systemic issues in the exam process.",
      "confidence": 0.95
