    {
      "title": "J'khand exam row: Students halt 26-day protest, give govt 2 months to act",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/j-khand-exam-row-students-halt-26-day-protest-give-govt-2-months-to-act-126081900945_1.html",
      "description": "Students protesting against alleged irregularities in Jharkhand recruitment exams on Wednesday suspended their 26-day agitation and gave a 2-month ultimatum to the state government to resolve issues.\nThe announcement comes a day after the JMM-led government issued notifications cancelling 22 recruitment exams and ordering a probe into 23 others conducted by the state public service commission and an outsourced agency since 2014.\n\"We are now suspending the stir and giving a two-month ultimatum to the government to resolve the issues and conduct a fair probe into recruitment exam irregularities,\" said a leader of the JPSC-JSSC Reforms Manch.\nThe manch, which led the students' agitation at Jaipal Singh Munda Stadium here, said three protesters - Rupesh Kumar Pal, Savita Kumari, Rahul Kranti - ended their 15-day fast on Wednesday.\nManch leader Ravindra Paswan said, \"The 26-day protest by students forced J'khand government to cancel 22 recruitment exams and launch a probe into 23 ...",
